{"content":[{"c":["ZELA, ZELAH*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["City of Benjamin’s tribe where the bones of Saul and Jonathan were buried (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.18.28","r":"Josh.18.28","rawR":"Josh.18.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.18.28","value":"Josh.18.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 18:28"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.21.14","r":"2Sam.21.14","rawR":"2Sam.21.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.21.14","value":"2Sam.21.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 21:14"},"). Zela was probably the native town of Saul’s father, Kish, and may well have been Saul’s home before he was anointed king."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"ZelaZelah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 18:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.18.28","rawQueryValue":"Josh.18.28","sourceRefExact":"Josh.18.28"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 21:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.21.14","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.21.14","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.21.14"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b9bfac227d3f867b0860df39e233be2e01c9b6e0180caa0e3842704703066f34","sourceItemName":"ZelaZelah","sourceItemOrder":65,"sourceMember":"Articles/Z.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"ZelaZelah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Zela, Zelah*","title":"Zela, Zelah*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}